Relevant columns & why they matter  

YES_ENERGY__SAMPLE_DATA.YES_ENERGY_SAMPLE.DART_PRICES_SAMPLE  
• "OBJECTID": filters on price‑node id (10000697078)  
• "DATETIME": join‑key for the hour of interest (2022‑10‑01)  
• "TIMEZONE": tells whether hour is CDT/CST ‑ needed for alignment  
• "DALMP": day‑ahead hub price ($/MWh)  
• "RTLMP": real‑time hub price ($/MWh)  

YES_ENERGY__SAMPLE_DATA.YES_ENERGY_SAMPLE.ISO_MARKET_TIMES_SAMPLE  
• "ISO": filter = 'ERCOT'  
• "DATETIME": join‑key to attach peak/off‑peak flags to each hour  
• "ONPEAK" | "OFFPEAK" | "WEPEAK" | "WDPEAK": peak classification flags  
• "MARKETDAY": helps verify the correct “market‑day” (2022‑10‑01)  
• "TIMEZONE": local time reference  

YES_ENERGY__SAMPLE_DATA.YES_ENERGY_SAMPLE.TS_FORECAST_SAMPLE  
• "OBJECTID": filter on load‑zone id (10000712973)  
• "DATATYPEID": distinguishes which forecast series is being pulled  
        19060 = hourly load forecast  
        9285  = wind generation forecast  
        662   = solar generation forecast  
• "DATETIME": forecast hour (matches price/load hours)  
• "VALUE": forecasted MW  
• "PUBLISHDATE": lets you see which vintage was used (optional insight)  
• "TIMEZONE": local time reference  

YES_ENERGY__SAMPLE_DATA.YES_ENERGY_SAMPLE.TS_LOAD_SAMPLE  
• "OBJECTID": filter 10000712973  
• "DATATYPEID": 9641 = actual hourly load  
• "DATETIME": hour ending stamp  
• "VALUE": actual load MW  
• "TIMEZONE": local time reference  

YES_ENERGY__SAMPLE_DATA.YES_ENERGY_SAMPLE.TS_GEN_SAMPLE  
• "OBJECTID": generation object that rolls up to same load‑zone  
• "DATATYPEID": 16  = actual wind gen ; 650 = actual solar gen  
• "DATETIME": hour stamp  
• "VALUE": actual gen MW  
• "TIMEZONE": local time reference  

Typical conditions that will be used  
• DATE("DATETIME") = '2022‑10‑01' (or BETWEEN '2022‑10‑01 00:00' AND '2022‑10‑02 00:00')  
• "OBJECTID" IN (10000697078, 10000712973 …)  
• "ISO" = 'ERCOT'  
• "DATATYPEID" IN (19060, 9285, 662, 9641, 16, 650)  

-----------------------------------------------------------------
